SUDOERS(5)                  File Formats

NAME
    sudoers - the rules of sudo

SYNOPSIS
    /etc/sudoers

DESCRIPTION
    /etc/sudoers contains the settings and the rules of sudo(1). It must
    belong to root with mode 0440, or sudo refuses to run. Text from # to
    the end of a line is a comment, except in #include, and a backslash at
    the end of a line continues it on the next one.

    A rule names who may run what, on which host and as whom.

        who host = (runas:group) [tag:] command, ...

    who is an account name, a group name preceded by %, a numeric id
    preceded by #, an alias or ALL. host is ALL on minios. runas lists
    the accounts that the command may run as, and group the groups. A
    command is a full path, optionally followed by the arguments it must
    be given, or ALL. The tag NOPASSWD: lets the command run without a
    password, and PASSWD: restores the question. When several rules
    match, the last one decides.

    Lines starting with Defaults change settings. Among them secure_path
    sets the PATH of commands, timestamp_timeout the minutes a time stamp
    remains valid (5 by default, 0 asks every time), passwd_tries the number
    of attempts (3), lecture whether the lecture is shown (once, always or
    never), env_keep the variables retained from the environment of the
    caller, and insults, targetpw and rootpw who is asked for which
    password. Aliases of the form User_Alias, Runas_Alias and Cmnd_Alias
    give a name to a list of accounts or commands.

    minios ships a file that lets root and the members of the group wheel
    run any command as any account with their own password.

        Defaults secure_path="/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin"
        root ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL
        %wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) ALL

    The file is part of the system image, while the membership of wheel
    is retained in /etc/group with the other account databases on the data
    volume (passwd(5)). The full description of the format is the
    sudoers manual of sudo 1.9.17p1, which is not installed.

EXAMPLES
    Defaults timestamp_timeout=15
    anna ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/pkg
    Cmnd_Alias POWER = /bin/initctl poweroff, /bin/initctl reboot
    %user ALL=(root) POWER

SEE ALSO
    sudo(1), doas.conf(5), passwd(5), index(7)
